                <pb facs="0773" n="697" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg697"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">651.5231/120: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-15T16:00:00+00:00">February 15, 1935—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 15—2:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>13. My telegram No. 11, January 30,3 p.m. Informed confidentially competent
                    official that quota passenger automobiles not trucks basis 1934 imports by
                    countries probable very soon as concession to French demand. However, American
                    assembly plants Barcelona would operate independently of quota. Customs returns
                    system enjoyed by <pb facs="0774" n="698" xml:id="pg698"/> France and United
                    Kingdom would be abolished. Imports duty to remain as is for all countries! If
                    this really goes through total 1934 imports of 13,641 units would be
                    automatically distributed by countries. 1934 imports by countries were as
                    follows: United States 472 units, Canada 2,789, France 3,815, United Kingdom
                    2,525, Germany 2,507, Italy 1,517, other countries 18.</p>
                <p>Commercial Attaché requests copy be sent Commerce.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
